The verifier error occurs because `bpf_dynptr_slice` attempts to read 9 bytes from a stack buffer that is only 8 bytes (`char buffer[8]`). This causes an out-of-bounds memory access, as the verifier detects an invalid read from offset `-24` (the buffer start) with size 9, exceeding the buffer's bounds.

The minimal fix is to change the size argument from 9 to 8, ensuring the requested slice fits within the buffer.

```diff
--- original.c
+++ fixed.c
@@ -10,7 +10,7 @@
 	char buffer[8] = {};
 	__u64 *data;

 	if (bpf_dynptr_from_skb(skb, 0, &ptr))
 		return 1;

-	data = bpf_dynptr_slice(&ptr, 0, buffer, 9);
+	data = bpf_dynptr_slice(&ptr, 0, buffer, 8);

 	return !!data;
 }
```
